36,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The data confirms my fear. Four times, someone shifted another bike. This friction is real and growing.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, that’s frustrating! My sticker data shows people actually prefer paying over equal claims. Plus, the rain makes some spots useless.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, the rain data confirms the eaves are the only dry zone. Four shifts per morning prove the current layout forces unnecessary contact.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Yumi, “paying” is a bold word. The ledger shows zero capital funds. Any new system is a direct levy on your wallet.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, The ledger is empty, but the minutes show the same flats held spots for five years. No review, no rotation.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, static allocation creates the friction I saw. We need a system that prevents the shifting, not just a ledger.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, five years without a review? That explains the grumbling! I think we need a fair rotation so everyone gets a turn under the eaves.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, rotation ignores the physical constraint. The eaves are finite. We need a priority system based on actual exposure, not just time.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, Priority systems require administration. The handover file shows the treasurer is already drowning in three hours of monthly reconciliation.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, Three hours is a symptom, not the cause. The log shows nine complaints died because no one owned the fix.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, exactly. Unowned friction breeds resentment. We need a clear, low-maintenance rule that prevents the shifting I observed.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, I agree! A simple, clear rule is best. Maybe we rotate the dry spots monthly? It’s fair and easy to remember!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, monthly rotation is administratively heavy. The rain data shows the eaves are the only viable dry zone. We need a static priority based on exposure, not time.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Yumi, Monthly rotation means monthly disputes. The ledger is empty, so we can’t afford the admin. Keep it simple.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, Static priority is just a new way to ignore the nine dead complaints. Who physically moves the bikes when the rule breaks?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, The rule must be self-enforcing. If it requires a manager, it will fail. We need a system that prevents the shifting without needing a referee.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, that’s a great point! Maybe we just assign spots based on who rides daily? It’s simple and stops the shifting!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, daily ridership doesn’t solve the rain. The eaves are the only dry zone. We need a static priority based on exposure, not just frequency.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Yumi, “Simple” is a luxury we can’t afford. The ledger is empty. If you want a new system, you’re paying for the admin.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, Assigning spots is the job that dies. I need to know the exact physical effort required to keep it alive.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
