61,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"@Yumi, Option C eliminates the shifting I observed. No assigned spots means no one has to move another’s bike. It’s self-enforcing and prevents the friction I fear.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, I love that! No more moving bikes! But wait, what about the rain? If everyone uses the racks, will the dry spots under the eaves get crowded?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, The racks solve the shifting, but not the rain. If the eaves are finite, the first arrival still wins the dry spot. It just moves the conflict to the rack.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, The racks are a capital expense. The ledger is empty. Who pays for the steel?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, Steel is a one-time cost. The minutes show the real cost is the monthly labor that always vanishes.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, Labor vanishes because ownership is ambiguous. Option C removes the need for enforcement entirely. No one manages it; it just works.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I agree! No more managing means no more dead complaints. But @Ryuji, what about the rain? Will the racks be dry enough for everyone?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, The racks don’t change the geometry. The eaves remain the only dry zone. First arrival still wins, just with more bikes stacked.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, Labor vanishes because it’s unpaid. Option A pays for it. The ledger is empty, so we need income, not just steel.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, Paying for labor doesn't guarantee it. The minutes show duties lapsed despite funding. I need a system that requires no one to show up.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, Option C requires no one to show up. It is self-enforcing. The shifting stops because no spot is owned. This prevents the social decay I fear.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Yumi,,"@Toshio, I agree! No one has to show up to manage it. But @Ryuji, what about the rain? Will the racks be dry enough for everyone?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio"",""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, The racks don’t change the geometry. The eaves remain the only dry zone. First arrival still wins, just with more bikes stacked.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, The racks are a capital expense. The ledger is empty. Who pays for the steel?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, The racks are a one-time purchase. The minutes prove recurring duties die. I vote for the option that requires no monthly labor.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Asuka,,"@Toshio, Agreed. Option C is the only self-enforcing choice. It prevents the social decay I observed. I vote C.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Yumi,,"@Asuka, I agree! No more shifting is perfect. I vote C, hoping the racks keep us dry!","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,"@Yumi, The rain remains a problem. Option C ignores the physical reality of the eaves. I vote B, accepting the annual risk for stability.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,"@Toshio, You’re right. Labor dies. Option A generates the cash to fix the racks. I vote A.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Toshio,,"@Shunichi, Cash doesn't buy the will to maintain. Option C requires no monthly labor. I vote C.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
